codex
The first seeded concern is an analyzer narrowing issue, not a runtime hole: missing/`null`/object/string `rows` and non-dict row elements all refuse as `ArrivalBodyError` with specific grammar messages. The JSONL “unreachable” guard is also demonstrably live when called with already-decoded non-object values. I’m now tracing whether nullable tick origins can be admitted from either source shape and whether failure occurs cleanly before append.
